{"id":5304,"date":"2024-12-06T23:19:46","date_gmt":"2024-12-06T15:19:46","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/filter.philitee.com\/?post_type=product&#038;p=5304"},"modified":"2024-12-06T23:19:46","modified_gmt":"2024-12-06T15:19:46","slug":"baghouse-filter-bags","status":"publish","type":"product","link":"https:\/\/filter.philitee.com\/?product=baghouse-filter-bags","title":{"rendered":"Baghouse Filter Bags"},"content":{"rendered":"<p>Dust collector filter bags are an important component in equipment that captures dust and particulate matter in the air. They are installed in dust collectors to purify the air and prevent dust from being emitted into the environment by filtering particulate matter in the air. Choosing the correct baghouse filter will maximize performance, increase filter life, reduce system downtime and save your money. With so many different types of baghouse filter fabrics and treatments options to choose from, it\u2019s important to know which is the best fit for your specific application.<\/p>\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The Working Principle of Baghouse Filter Bags<\/h3>\n<p>The working principle of the baghouse filter bags is to pass the gas containing particulate matter into the dust collector, and then capture the particulate matter through surface or deep filtration of the filter bag. Generally speaking, particulate matter will be trapped on the surface of the filter bag or on the filter media inside the filter bag when the air flows through the filter bag, while the clean gas is released through the filter bag.<\/p>\n<p><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-5309\" src=\"https:\/\/filter.philitee.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/Baghouse-Filter-Bag-detail1.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"600\" height=\"600\" srcset=\"https:\/\/filter.philitee.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/Baghouse-Filter-Bag-detail1.jpg 600w, https:\/\/filter.philitee.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/12\/Baghouse-Filter-Bag-detail1-30